Z||000000||JayUSA77||07-04-2001||09:09 PM||||Hey does anyone know what is the offset for the fiero wheels.  In other words what 5 bolts will fit on and what 5 bolt wheels wont. Im looking to buy some off ebay and if i buy them and they dont fit ill be pis$ed off.<BR>-J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||3
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||07-04-2001||09:20 PM||||Found this list in a search last week on here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>BUICK<BR>SKYHAWK, SKYLARK, 88-UP<BR>SOMERSET<BR>CADILLAC<BR>CIMARRON 81-88<BR>CHEVY<BR>BERETTA, CORSICA 87-97<BR>GTU, GTZ, Z-26 89-97<BR>CAVALIER 81-UP<BR>Z24 89-UP<BR>CELEBRITY 82-90<BR>CITATION 80-85<BR>X-11 81-85<BR>MALIBU, CHEVELLE 97-UP<BR>CHRYSLER<BR>LEBARON 86-95<BR>LASER, GTS 85-88<BR>NEW YORKER 86-93<BR>SEBRING CONVERTIBLE 96-UP<BR>DODGE<BR>ARIES, 400, 600 86-88<BR>DAYTONA, TURBO Z 85-93<BR>DYNASTY 88-93<BR>LANCER 85-89<BR>SHADOW 87-94<BR>SPIRIT 89-94<BR>STRATUS 95-UP<BR>LEXUS<BR>ES, 250 90-93<BR>OLDSMOBILE<BR>ACHIEVA 92-97<BR>CUTLASS CALAIS, 82-89<BR>CIERA, FIRENZA<BR>PLYMOUTH<BR>ACCLAIM 89-95<BR>BREEZE 95-UP<BR>CARAVELLE 85-88<BR>LASER 85-89<BR>RS, TURBO 85-89<BR>NEON 5-LUG 95-99<BR>RELIANT, TOURISMO 85-89<BR>SUNDANCE 87-94<BR>PONTIAC<BR>6000, LE 82-90<BR>FIERO, GT 84-88<BR>GRANDAM 85-98<BR>SE, GT 85-98<BR>SUNBIRD, J2000 82-94<BR>SUNFIRE GT 95-UP<BR>TOYOTA<BR>CAMRY 86-91<BR>CELICA 92-00<BR>VOLKSWAGEN<BR>BEETLE 99-UP<BR>CORRADO VR6 92-93<BR>JETTAIII (4CYL) 99-UP<BR>JETTAIII VR6 93-UP<BR>GLX VR6 92-98<BR>GOLF 2000<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||saleenfiero||07-04-2001||09:22 PM||||5X100MM is the bolt pattern.  I guess you can have a TINY amount of leeway when it comes to offest, but I thought the fiero rim was 40MM offset.  Anybody got real answers?||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||07-04-2001||09:52 PM||||40MM will work but I believe it is 35MM on the '84, 37MM on the '85 through '87 and 37MM on the '88 rear (7" rim). The '88 front is 32MM (6.5" rim) -- this is from memory and mine isn't always correct...........||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||07-04-2001||10:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>40MM will work but I believe it is 35MM on the '84, 37MM on the '85 through '87 and 37MM on the '88 rear (7" rim). The '88 front is 32MM (6.5" rim) -- this is from memory and mine isn't always correct...........</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Gotta question. So if I went with a wheel that had a 40mm offset, would that make my wheels stick out a bit, or in?<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumsig.JPG">      <BR>84 SE (FOR SALE)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)(take it off my hands for $50)<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE sometime in this summer)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||07-04-2001||11:02 PM||||sqoach, slightly out but, most of the 17" wheels you see on Fieros are a 40MM offset......here is a picture of George Miller's Green '88 GT with 17" 40MM wheels.....<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-870f.jpg">  <P>OOPS!! wrong picture (well......the wheel <I>is</I> sticking out!!) - actually he broke an upper ball joint!<P>Here is the one I meant.......<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-219f.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 07-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||07-04-2001||11:05 PM||||You'll only notice that on '88s. Earlier years used the same offset all the way around.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||JayUSA77||07-06-2001||01:52 AM||||so would any 5 bolt fit on our cars.?????  Its just a matter of sticking in our out right.  I wanna put momo 5 bolts. do you think they will go on without a problem.<BR>-J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||tgowens||07-06-2001||02:08 AM||||you can only use wheels that use the 5 X 100MM bolt pattern........that means that there are five bolts 100MM apart...that's why a 5 X 115 (for example) won't work, it won't bolt up to the hub.......||||reg||1
